#current-chapter.update("Appendix E: Practical Skills")
= Appendix E — Practical Skills Checklist

These exercises reinforce concepts taught in the volume. Use equipment only with permission and follow its maker's and your institution's safety rules. Do not use private data in a shared practice folder.

== E.1 Create and Organise

+ Create a folder named `Computer-practice` in a permitted location.
+ Make a short text document and save it with a descriptive name.
+ Create a subfolder; copy the document into it and verify that the original remains.
+ Rename the copy. Observe that renaming does not convert its file format.
+ Save a separate backup according to the local policy and verify that it can be opened.

== E.2 Try a Spreadsheet

+ Enter 12 and 8 into cells A1 and A2. Enter `=A1+A2` in A3 and check that the result is 20.
+ Enter a rate in D1. Construct a formula using `$D$1`, copy it down and inspect whether the reference remains fixed.
+ Repeat with a relative reference and observe the change. Program behaviour and syntax may vary; consult the software's help.

== E.3 Inspect a Network Safely

+ Identify the local connection as wired or wireless without changing settings.
+ Explain the difference between connecting to local Wi-Fi and reaching the internet.
+ Identify a browser and a search engine. Verify an official address independently before entering sensitive information.

== E.4 Troubleshoot in Order

+ Describe the symptom and note when it began.
+ Check safe external causes such as power, connections and device status.
+ Test one change at a time and record the result.
+ Stop and escalate electrical hazards or internal repairs to qualified personnel.
+ Verify that the original problem is resolved and document the outcome.

#trap-box("Safety before speed")[
  Do not open a power supply, handle exposed live wiring or use water on energised equipment. A practical exercise must not put the learner or the device at risk.
]
